{
  "schema": 1,
  "scope": "MLX-CUDA and llama.cpp measurements on NVIDIA GB10 (DGX Spark), cross-platform numerics vs M5 Metal, gated-delta kernel and qmm patch experiments; scripts and gzipped raw JSON/logs.",
  "caveats": [
    "Single box type (GB10 sm_121); all speed runs on DGX Spark A except noted MLX source builds.",
    "Five timed reps per harness cell; dense decode ratios can move by several points between sessions.",
    "No Darkbloom provider serving on Linux; mlx-swift builds on GB10 only with local workarounds (see report), mlx-swift-lm needs local platform guards, and 8 of 12 provider-swift targets fail at their first Apple-only dependency.",
    "Client-side throughput timing; not coordinator or HTTP serving measurements.",
    "4-bit MLX vs GGUF formats differ; greedy cross-engine token match is not a numerics gate.",
    "Swift build uses clang 21 with CUDA 13.0 via -allow-unsupported-compiler (unsupported pair); Swift output was checked against Python MLX-CUDA tokens."
  ],
